---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Events
seoTitle: Niwot Events Calendar | TownofNiwot.com
description: Confirmed events in Niwot, Colorado — concerts, art walks, dances and seasonal gatherings — each one checked against the organizer's own page.
navKey: events
permalink: /events/
ogImage: whistle-stop-caboose.jpg
ogImageAlt: The red CB&Q 14649 caboose at Whistle Stop Park, strung with festoon lighting
footMetaRight: Dates read from each organizer’s page
needsEvents: true
scripts:
  - /assets/js/page-events.js
pageStyles: |
  .n-evrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.42fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(24px,3vw,56px);align-items:start}
  /* The upcoming list: one row per occurrence — date and time, then the
     event, then its action. The cards the homepage uses are the same markup. */
  .n-uplist{display:grid;gap:0;margin-top:clamp(18px,2vw,28px)}
  .n-uplist .n-up{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,.3fr) minmax(0,1fr) auto;gap:8px 24px;align-items:start;padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--n-rule)}
  .n-uplist .n-up:first-child{border-top:3px solid var(--n-red)}
  .n-uplist .n-up .n-h3{font-size:1.25rem !important}
  .n-uplist .n-up .n-jump{grid-column:3;grid-row:1 / span 3;align-self:center}
  .n-uplist .n-up > .n-label{grid-column:1;grid-row:1 / span 3}
  .n-uplist .n-up > .n-h3,.n-uplist .n-up > .n-body,.n-uplist .n-up > .n-small{grid-column:2}
  .n-fold{margin-top:clamp(22px,2.6vw,36px);border-top:2px solid var(--n-evergreen)}
  .n-fold > summary{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:14px;min-height:56px;padding:14px 0;list-style:none;cursor:pointer;color:var(--n-evergreen)}
  .n-fold > summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
  .n-fold > summary:hover{color:var(--n-red-ink)}
  .n-fold > summary .n-gmark{display:inline-block;width:12px;height:12px;border-right:2px solid currentColor;border-bottom:2px solid currentColor;transform:rotate(45deg);transition:transform .18s ease;flex:none;margin-right:4px}
  .n-fold[open] > summary .n-gmark{transform:rotate(-135deg)}
  .n-cal{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,.8fr);gap:clamp(24px,3vw,56px);align-items:start;padding-top:8px}
  .n-grid7{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,minmax(0,1fr));border-left:1px solid var(--n-rule);border-top:1px solid var(--n-rule)}
  .n-dow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,minmax(0,1fr))}
  [data-day]{display:block;width:100%;min-height:clamp(56px,7vw,92px);padding:8px;background:var(--n-white);border:0;border-right:1px solid var(--n-rule);border-bottom:1px solid var(--n-rule);color:var(--n-ink);font:inherit;text-align:left;cursor:default}
  button[data-day][data-has="yes"]{cursor:pointer;background:#EEE7D9}
  button[data-day][data-has="yes"]:hover{background:#E2D9C4}
  button[data-day][aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--n-evergreen);color:var(--n-white)}
  button[data-day][aria-pressed="true"] .n-daytag{color:var(--n-gold-lt)}
  [data-day][data-empty="yes"]{background:transparent;border-right-color:transparent}
  .n-daytag{display:block;margin-top:6px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--n-red-ink)}
  button[data-nav]{padding:11px 16px;background:transparent;border:2px solid var(--n-evergreen);color:var(--n-evergreen);font:inherit;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;cursor:pointer;transition:background .2s ease,color .2s ease}
  button[data-nav]:hover{background:var(--n-evergreen);color:var(--n-white)}
  .n-detail{position:sticky;top:88px}
  /* A sticky rail is only sticky against something scrolling beside it. Once
     the calendar stacks, it would just pin itself over the page. */
  @media (max-width:900px){.n-evrow,.n-cal{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.n-detail{position:static}}
  /* "View details" is a bare button, so it misses the touch padding guide.css
     gives .n-link. 22px is not a tap target. The padding lives here rather
     than in the inline style calendar-core.js writes, because an inline style
     wins over a media query and the button would stay 22px on a phone. */
  .n-jump{padding:0}
  @media (max-width:1080px){.n-jump{padding-top:12px;padding-bottom:12px}}
  /* A seventh of a phone screen is about 34px of usable cell, and the series
     name is clipped to "MARKI". Below this width the name stays in the
     accessible name of the day button and a square marker carries it
     visually, matched by the shaded ground and explained under the grid. */
  @media (max-width:620px){
  .n-uplist .n-up{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}
  .n-uplist .n-up > .n-label,.n-uplist .n-up > .n-h3,.n-uplist .n-up > .n-body,.n-uplist .n-up > .n-small,.n-uplist .n-up .n-jump{grid-column:1;grid-row:auto}
  .n-uplist .n-up .n-jump{align-self:start}
  button[data-day]{position:relative;padding:6px 4px}
  .n-daytag{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap;border:0}
  button[data-day][data-has="yes"]::after{content:"";display:block;width:9px;height:9px;margin-top:6px;background:var(--n-red)}
  button[data-day][aria-pressed="true"]::after{background:var(--n-gold-lt)}
  }
  /* A day with several events: a compact list, one expanded. The items are
     buttons in the browser and plain text in the build. */
  .n-daypick{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;width:100%;padding:11px 0 11px 12px;background:none;border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--n-rule);border-left:3px solid transparent;color:var(--n-ink);font:inherit;font-size:.9375rem;line-height:1.4;text-align:left}
  button.n-daypick{cursor:pointer}
  button.n-daypick:hover{color:var(--n-red-ink)}
  .n-daypick[aria-pressed="true"],.n-daypick[aria-current="true"]{border-left-color:var(--n-red);color:var(--n-evergreen)}
  .n-expected{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
  @media (max-width:620px){.n-expected li{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) !important}}
---
<section class="n-bg-white" aria-labelledby="title-h">
<div class="n-wrap" style="padding-top:clamp(28px,4vw,60px);padding-bottom:clamp(20px,2.5vw,36px)">
<div class="n-g2-wide" style="align-items:end">
<div>
<div class="n-label">Events</div>
<h1 class="n-display" id="title-h" style="margin-top:14px;font-size:clamp(2.5rem,1.8rem + 3.4vw,5rem);line-height:.96;max-width:14ch;color:var(--n-evergreen)">What&#8217;s happening in Niwot</h1>
</div>
<p class="n-lead" style="margin:0;max-width:50ch">Concerts, art walks and gatherings, with the organizer named on every entry. A date appears here only once it has been read on the organizer&#8217;s own page, and each entry links there. Times are Mountain Time.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

{#- The upcoming list beside the one photograph. Rendered at build time,
    recomputed from the real date on load. -#}
<section class="n-bg-paper n-pad-sm" aria-labelledby="next-h" style="border-top:1px solid var(--n-rule);border-bottom:1px solid var(--n-rule)">
<div class="n-wrap">
<div class="n-evrow">
<div>
<figure style="margin:0">
{% photo "whistle-stop-caboose.jpg", "The red CB&Q 14649 caboose on a short length of track at Whistle Stop Park, strung with festoon lighting", "(max-width: 900px) calc(100vw - 40px), (max-width: 1440px) 36vw, 500px", "display:block;width:100%;height:clamp(200px,24vw,340px);object-fit:cover;object-position:center 52%", true %}
<figcaption class="n-cap">Whistle Stop Park &#8212; the lawn beside the caboose, where most of it happens</figcaption>
</figure>
<p class="n-small" style="margin:18px 0 0;max-width:46ch">This is a curated list, not the whole calendar: the Niwot Business Association&#8217;s calendar carries everything the organizers publish. An entry is added here only after its date has been read on the organizer&#8217;s page; past events leave the list on their own.</p>
<div class="n-btns" style="margin-top:16px">
<a class="n-btn" href="https://niwot.com/upcoming-events/" rel="noopener">Full community calendar <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
<a class="n-btn n-btn--ghost" href="/contact/">Submit an event</a>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<div class="n-shead n-shead-row" style="border-bottom-color:var(--n-evergreen)">
<h2 class="n-h2" id="next-h" style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,1.2rem + 1.2vw,2.25rem);color:var(--n-evergreen)">Upcoming events</h2>
<span class="n-label n-label--quiet">Mountain Time</span>
</div>
<div class="n-uplist" data-upcoming="select">{{ eventsBuild.upcomingEventsHtml | safe }}</div>

{#- The month grid and its detail rail, folded. "View details" above and
    the homepage cards open it on the chosen day and event. -#}
<details class="n-fold" id="calendar" data-cal-fold>
<summary><span class="n-h3" id="cal-h" style="font-size:clamp(1.25rem,1.1rem + .6vw,1.5rem)">Month view</span><span style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px"><span class="n-label n-label--quiet" data-cal-label aria-live="polite">{{ eventsBuild.monthLabel }}</span><span class="n-gmark" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></summary>
<div class="n-cal">
<div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px 20px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding-bottom:16px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--n-evergreen)">
<button type="button" data-cal-today hidden style="padding:0;background:none;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;color:var(--n-sky-ink);font:inherit;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;cursor:pointer">This month</button>
<div style="display:flex;gap:10px">
<button type="button" data-nav data-cal-prev aria-label="Previous month">&#8592; Prev</button>
<button type="button" data-nav data-cal-next aria-label="Next month">Next <span aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></button>
</div>
</div>
<div class="n-dow" style="margin-top:14px" aria-hidden="true">
{%- for d in eventsBuild.dows %}
<div class="n-label n-label--quiet" style="padding:0 8px 8px;font-size:12px">{{ d }}</div>
{%- endfor %}
</div>
<div class="n-grid7" data-cal-grid role="group" aria-label="Month">{{ eventsBuild.cellsHtml | safe }}</div>
<p class="n-small" style="margin:16px 0 0">Shaded days &#8212; marked with a square on a narrow screen &#8212; carry a confirmed event. Select one for the detail. The detail beside the grid always belongs to the month shown.</p>
</div>
<aside class="n-detail" aria-labelledby="detail-h">
<h3 class="n-label n-label--quiet" id="detail-h" style="margin:0;padding-bottom:14px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--n-evergreen)">Event detail</h3>
{#- With nothing selected it shows the next upcoming occurrence. -#}
<div data-cal-detail style="padding-top:20px">{{ eventsBuild.detailHtml | safe }}</div>
</aside>
</div>
</details>

{#- Annual events the organizer has not yet dated, folded. Nothing in it is
    a scheduled date, and none of it enters the list above or the
    structured data. -#}
<details class="n-fold" id="expected">
<summary><span class="n-h3" id="exp-h" style="font-size:clamp(1.25rem,1.1rem + .6vw,1.5rem)">Annual events still waiting on a date</span><span style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px"><span class="n-label n-label--quiet">{{ eventsBuild.expectedCount }}</span><span class="n-gmark" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></summary>
<p class="n-small" style="margin:0;max-width:60ch">Expected &#8212; date not confirmed. These recur every year but the organizer has not yet published this season&#8217;s dates.</p>
<ul class="n-expected" data-expected>{{ eventsBuild.expectedHtml | safe }}</ul>
</details>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
